  "question": {
    "text": "$\\int \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{\\mathrm{x}} \\mathrm{dx}$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "JfcVP",
      "text": "$(x+1) \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x}+C$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZSZjJ",
      "text": "$x \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x}+C$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RdAbe",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{x}-x \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}+C$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lJ7Vf",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{x}-(x+1) \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}+C$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $I=\\int 1 \\cdot \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{\\mathrm{x}} \\mathrm{dx}$<br />Using by parts,<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />I & =\\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x} \\cdot(x)-\\int \\frac{1}{1+x} \\times \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x}} \\times x d x \\\\<br />& =x \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x} \\cdot-\\int \\frac{x}{(1+x) 2 \\sqrt{x}} d x \\\\<br />& =x \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}-\\int\\left(\\frac{1+x}{(1+x) 2 \\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{(1+x) 2 \\sqrt{x}}\\right) d x \\\\<br />& =x \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}-\\int \\frac{d x}{2 \\sqrt{x}}+\\int \\frac{d x}{2 \\sqrt{x}(1+x)} \\\\<br />& =x \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x}+\\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}+C \\\\<br />& =(x+1) \\tan ^{-1} \\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x}+C<br />\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
